## PATTERN 1: <Imperative rule title>

**RULE:** The rule, its reason, its source (`doc:line`), and the failure mode it prevents ("will silently mark rows synced on every failure").

**CANONICAL EXAMPLE** (`path/file.ts:lines`):
```ts
// the real shipped snippet, with the comment that names the trap
```
Why this example is the bar, in 1–2 sentences. If a test enforces the rule, say so and cite it.

**ANTI-PATTERN:** the literal wrong code or copy, why it looks fine, how it fails downstream, and the helper to use instead.

(Optional) **CARVE-OUT:** a narrowly sanctioned exception: who ruled it, the date, and the exact boundary ("sanctioned there, and only there").

